{%- comment -%}
  snippets/thumbnail.liquid
  ============================================
  Compact card: image + title + price/subtitle + an "Add to cart"
  button. Named generically (not "product-thumbnail") because the
  plan is to reuse this shape for more than tagged products later —
  e.g. branded collab / influencer / creator channel cards — not
  just plain product data.

  Click handling for [data-thumbnail-add] is fully self-contained in
  assets/thumbnail.js (event delegation on document), so nothing that
  renders this snippet needs to wire anything up itself — just make
  sure assets/thumbnail.css and assets/thumbnail.js are both loaded
  on the page. Today's only caller is snippets/video-card.liquid's
  "card outside video" CTA style.

  PARAMS:
    product     — required, a product object
    variant     — optional, defaults to
                  product.selected_or_first_available_variant
    image_width — optional, defaults to 200

  Usage:
    {% render 'thumbnail', product: product %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign variant = variant | default: product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign image_width = image_width | default: 200
-%}
<div class="thumbnail">
  <a class="thumbnail__link" href="{{ product.url }}">
    {%- if product.featured_image -%}
      {{
        product.featured_image
        | image_url: width: image_width
        | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', class: 'thumbnail__image', alt: product.title
      }}
    {%- endif -%}
    <span class="thumbnail__info">
      <span class="thumbnail__title">{{ product.title }}</span>
      <span class="thumbnail__price">{{ variant.price | money }}</span>
    </span>
  </a>

  {%- if variant.available -%}
    <button
      type="button"
      class="thumbnail__add"
      data-thumbnail-add
      data-variant-id="{{ variant.id }}"
    >
      Add to cart
    </button>
  {%- else -%}
    <button type="button" class="thumbnail__add" disabled>Sold out</button>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
